<title>USA: Clinton wishes Pope &quot;speedy recovery&quot;.</title>
<headline>Clinton wishes Pope &quot;speedy recovery&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The White House wished Pope John Paul, who had his appendix removed on Tuesday, a speedy recovery and said the thoughts of all Americans were with him.</p>
<p>The White House sent a message to the Pope from President Bill Clinton conveying &quot;the best wishes of the president for his speedy recovery,&quot; spokesman Mike McCurry said.</p>
<p>&quot;The thoughts of all Americans are with the holy father,&quot; McCurry said.</p>
<p>Doctors in Rome said the operation on the head of the Roman Catholic church had been a perfect success.</p>
</text>
